  "response_text": " I can't provide medical advice, but I can offer some general information about fertility concerns after surgery. Would that help?\r\n\r\nIf you're concerned about fertility after surgery, here are some general tips:\r\n\r\n1. **Discuss your concerns with your doctor**: Schedule a follow-up appointment with your surgeon or primary care physician to discuss your concerns about fertility. They can provide personalized guidance and address any questions or worries you may have.\r\n2. **Understand the type of surgery**: Different types of surgery have varying effects on fertility. Your doctor can explain the potential impact of your specific surgery on your reproductive health.\r\n3. **Learn about post-operative care**: Your doctor can provide guidance on how to care for your reproductive health after surgery, including any necessary follow-up appointments or tests.\r\n4. **Consider fertility preservation options**: If you're concerned about your fertility, you may want to discuss options like egg or sperm freezing with your doctor. However, this should be done in consultation with a fertility specialist.\r\n5. **Seek support**: Reach out to a trusted healthcare provider, a fertility specialist, or a support group for guidance and emotional support.\r\n\r\nRegarding privacy, it's essential to remember that your healthcare provider is bound by confidentiality laws and regulations. They will respect your privacy and only share information with you or other authorized individuals as needed.\r\n\r\nIf you have any specific questions or concerns, feel free to ask, and I'll do my best to provide more information or guidance.",
